														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4858900">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Containment procedures, description, an addendum or two, and 2 ethics committee reports</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A man with severely burned skin who claims to have gone to the Christian hell. His skin will anomalously smolder and catch on fire at random intervals.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> One day, a man drenched in fire ran out of a burning building. It took a while to put him out and calm him down, but it was a mystery as to how he survived. The Foundation was alerted when his burns refused to heal and even got hotter, sometimes causing fires.</p>
<p>The man claimed to be Junior Toure, an Angolan man who died 67 years before he was found by The Foundation. His skin stayed burned and caught on fire randomly, but that was easily dealt with in the form of automatic sprinklers.</p>
<p>The man claimed to have gone to what he believed to be the Christian interpretation of hell, claiming to have seen glimpses of an endless field with people laying on the ground, bound by chains, forever on fire, the flames growing ever hotter.</p>
<p>He was in constant pain. He cried regularly and screams could be heard from his cell for hours on end. There was no way to help him. Eventually, a grievance with the ethics committee was filed, asking them if he should be put out of his misery. After an interview, he said &quot;I don't want that. I don't want to return.&quot;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Toure aged normally, and as he did, his mental state deteriorated. He became paranoid and erratic, fearing death and a return to that hellish place. He died insane, with the only resemblance of peace being him requesting that his body be put in the ocean, saying &quot;It might dull the pain while I'm down there.&quot;</p>
<p>His body burned nonstop after he died, with nothing being able to stop it. It eventually turned into a pile of ash. Another ethics committee grievance was filed, asking for Toure's last wish to be granted. The committee stipulated that if the ash had no anomalous properties, then it was to be dispersed in the Pacific Ocean.</p>
<p>The ash was found to be non-anomalous, and the dead man's wish was fulfilled. His ashes found their way to the bottom of the ocean, bearing a stark contrast to what he was bound to for eternity to come.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> It's a very dark SCP, which is nothing new, but it would also be a neutralized SCP.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
</div>
